# Whether the Stripe payment path is offered at checkout.
# false -> "Checkout — Payment" (design frame DOtD2)
# true  -> the Stripe step in the cart drawer (design frame hed4V)
# PUBLIC: compiled into the bundle. Never put a secret key in an NG_APP_* var.
NG_APP_STRIPE_ENABLED=false

# Base path every gateway call hangs off. RELATIVE on purpose, and effectively
# fixed: nothing in this repo sends CORS headers, so the browser must stay
# same-origin. nginx (apps/web/nginx.conf) and `ng serve`
# (apps/web/proxy.conf.mjs) both proxy /v1 through to the API gateway.
# PUBLIC like every NG_APP_*, but there is nothing secret in a path.
NG_APP_API_GATEWAY_URL=/v1

# Whether the address autocomplete is offered at checkout. A FLAG ONLY — the
# Geoapify API key is NOT here and must never be: an NG_APP_* value is compiled
# into the bundle and readable in devtools. The key is server-side, read from
# GEOAPIFY_API_KEY in .env.local.web (CUSTOM box) by nginx in the container and
# by apps/web/proxy.conf.mjs under `ng serve`.
#
# Turning this on takes BOTH halves, and each fails silently without the other:
#   1. this flag = true, then RESTART the dev server (NG_APP_* is build-time)
#   2. GEOAPIFY_API_KEY set in .env.local.web's CUSTOM box
# Flag off with a valid key: no suggestions, and the proxy still answers 200.
# Flag on with no key: the proxy answers 503 rather than calling Geoapify
# unauthenticated. Get a free key at https://myprojects.geoapify.com
NG_APP_GEOCODE_ENABLED=false

# Host-facing realtime WebSocket URL, e.g.
# ws://localhost:4566/ws/<apiId>/<stage>.
#
# Nothing bridges .env.local.web to this file: copy WS_URL out of
# ../../.env.local.web (regenerated by `make env-file` from Terraform's ws_url
# output, and reminted on every apply) and paste it below. Leaving it blank
# starts the app with no socket at all; app-config.ts logs a console.warn
# naming this variable rather than failing, so check the browser console when
# toasts and the live unread badge never appear.
#
# CONTRACT: This is the HOST-facing url, NOT WS_MANAGEMENT_ENDPOINT. That one is
# the in-network publish endpoint and answers a browser handshake with an S3 XML
# body rather than an endpoint error. Empty leaves the socket unopened, so
# notifications arrive only on the next page load.
# PUBLIC like every NG_APP_*, and the token rides the query string per
# connection — never put a token here.
NG_APP_WS_URL=

# Whether the browser OpenTelemetry SDK boots at all — traces (document load,
# navigation, gateway calls joined via traceparent), Web Vitals, and JS
# errors, all sent same-origin to /otlp and on to OpenObserve.
#
# Off by default. Turning it on takes TWO things:
#   1. this flag = true, then RESTART the dev server (NG_APP_* is build-time)
#   2. `make observability-up` — the collector sits behind compose's
#      `observability` profile; a plain `make up` leaves it down
# Flag on with the collector down: every export fails silently (a failed
# export does not break the app), so nothing but a browser devtools network
# error signals it. Flag off (or unset): the SDK never boots — zero requests
# to /otlp — and costs nothing, so this is the only NG_APP_* flag that warns
# on nothing when unset.
# PUBLIC like every NG_APP_*, and there is no secret in a boolean.
NG_APP_RUM_ENABLED=false
